microsoft.com Microsoft builds AI-powered platforms, tools, and services for consumers, businesses, and governments. Beginning in fiscal 2027 it reports two segments. Agents and Infra is the dominant segment. It includes:
- the Azure cloud and AI infrastructure platform;
- Microsoft 365 commercial and consumer cloud productivity subscriptions;
- productivity and server licensing;
- industry solutions;
- frontier and support services. Devices and Consumer includes:
- search and advertising;
- Xbox gaming content, services, and hardware;
- Windows OEM licensing and devices. The company's Microsoft Cloud offerings generate a large and growing share of revenue, backed by a substantial commercial remaining performance obligation. Microsoft is investing heavily in data center and AI infrastructure to meet demand for AI and agent workloads, and it holds an investment in OpenAI that materially affects reported GAAP earnings. Its stated mission is to empower every person and every organization on the planet to achieve more, with a focus on making AI broadly available and responsible. Updated Oct 28, 2026 The concentration bears get a direct rebuttal here: Balchunas argues the megacaps function as a far broader basket than seven tickers because of 850 acquisitions, with Alphabet's YouTube alone big enough to rank 19th in the US if spun out. If you own the index, you own that argument either way. A 7% intraday slide far exceeds what partners did today, with Google and Meta both off less than 3%. No confirmed catalyst behind the gap. An OpenAI board member publicly calling for labs to stop advancing pre-training and RL is a governance risk the AI trade has not priced. The argument that frontier security is weak enough for weights to be stolen mid-explosion gives Washington a concrete reason to regulate compute and model releases. Service is back, but the outage lands while UK regulators move to put major cloud providers under financial-sector oversight, making downtime a policy risk for Microsoft. The practical call is positioning: own more cyclicals when business is booming and lean on staples and drugmakers when growth rolls over. Cramer says sector membership now drives well over half of a stock's move thanks to sector ETFs, so being in the wrong camp costs you even when the company executes. The defensive rotation argument got concrete here: if AI capex peaks in 2027, the picks-and-shovels trade loses its bid first and staples absorb the flows. The desk's valuation game landed the same way, favoring Deere, Coca-Cola and Johnson & Johnson over richly priced tech, and few on the panel believe Nike's new CEO reverses share losses at next week's investor day. The concrete call here is on Take-Two: Palmeri frames GTA 6 as a $3 billion opening act and the company as the last dominant pure-play publisher as the industry consolidates. The Nvidia segment cuts the other way, with leadership now interim and a federal espionage probe running into an earnings report. The bull case now rests entirely on Nvidia's engineers rather than its frontman: reporters argue the chips, CUDA and the customer queue outlast Huang, while analysts have yet to downgrade. The open risk is relational, since supplier ties in Korea and Taiwan were personal, and Washington scrutiny of chips reaching Chinese users through offshore neoclouds is only starting. The energy drink debate lands on whether Celsius's two-thirds drawdown from a 28,000% run is a broken story or a reset entry into a $25 billion category. On the picks side, Lakin's contrarian read is that insurance brokers stand to gain from AI, and that only 35 million people cruise versus 100 million visiting Disney World and Vegas. As of Sep 30, 2026 · disclosed Nov 13, 2026 · ~45 days stale — may not reflect current positions. Alex Sacerdote's Whale Rock, up nearly 73% this year on tech bets, disclosed Microsoft as a new position as of September 30, making it roughly 3.9% of the portfolio. Apple was among four names no longer reported at quarter-end, alongside fresh stakes in Salesforce, HPE and Okta. Shares of Microsoft (NASDAQ:MSFT | MSFT Price Prediction) trade near $521 after a rough week. The 24/7 Wall St. price target sits at $648.94, suggesting 24.6% upside over the next 12 months.… An income base is the core of a retirement portfolio: the small group of holdings you expect to pay you every quarter for decades, through recessions, rate cycles, and bear markets. That… IREN has a backlog above $20 billion, a Microsoft anchor deal, and Wall Street targets north of $99. It also has a $6 billion funding hole and a missed milestone. Which story… FAA Administrator Bryan Bedford gave a frank assessment after the latest air traffic disruption. The nation’s aging control system “will continue to break” until it is replaced, he said. He also named… Michael Burry has spent the past year arguing that the AI boom rests on a flattering accounting choice. In his Substack, Cassandra Unchained, he called the practice of stretching the assumed lives… Harvard's endowment rotated inside AI chips just before a brutal selloff hit one of them. Since then, the two stocks have moved very differently, and a closer look at the filing shows… SpaceX (NASDAQ:SPCX | SPCX Price Prediction) has reportedly cut most of the team behind its AI video generator. The Information reported on November 13 that SpaceX’s artificial intelligence division laid off approximately… A raised outlook and a new hyperscaler cloud deal from Cerebras Systems (NASDAQ:CBRS) are driving a sharp rebound in the leveraged ETF tied to the AI chipmaker. Leverage Shares 2X Long CBRS… JEPI owners already trust JPMorgan with their retirement cash, yet a cheaper sibling from the same firm sits mostly ignored. It trails JEPI in one key area, and that gap decides who… A billionaire bond investor is sounding alarms about what he calls a hollow tree at the center of the stock market, and the numbers hiding beneath the S&P 500's record highs suggest… Microsoft keeps raising its dividend while pouring cash into AI data centers at a record pace. Can shareholder payouts survive a spending race that now rivals the company's free cash flow? Wall Street analysts are unanimous on Broadcom, yet the loudest skeptics sit on CNBC, and the stock has dropped after beating earnings before. Financing risks, supply limits, and a split in institutional… Microsoft just edged past NVIDIA in market value by a margin that could vanish in one session. The cloud numbers behind the stock, and the spending that could undercut them, tell a… Nvidia is bouncing back after its CEO's shocking exit, but a bond market flashing a number not seen in years and one inflation report due Friday could still wreck Wall Street's best… An outage at Microsoft (NASDAQ:MSFT | MSFT Price Prediction) is pushing buyers toward the biggest independent names in cybersecurity. CrowdStrike Holdings (NASDAQ:CRWD) stock is at $237.30 in morning trading, up 3%. That… Microsoft builds AI-powered platforms, tools, and services for consumers, businesses, and governments. Beginning in fiscal 2027 it reports two segments. 24/7 Wall St.'s 12-month price target for MSFT is $651.47, rated Buy. The Wall Street consensus target is $636.12.									MSFT price prediction → This post may contain links from our sponsors and affiliates, and Flywheel Publishing may receive compensation for actions taken through them.				© 2026 24/7 Wall St.
